From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 04:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] misc: call the driver open outside misc_mtx, plus MISCDBG tracing

This is the kernel that is running on the device (uname #4). Two changes
in one patch, kept together because the tracing is what proved the fix
was needed and is what identified the holder.

1. Scope fix. Stock misc_open() - mainline 4.14 and current master alike,
   this is NOT a Samsung deviation - holds the global misc_mtx across the
   driver's own f_op->open(). One driver whose open blocks forever
   therefore freezes every misc-device open on the system: mali0, ion,
   binder, hwbinder, uinput, the compositor and every Android HAL. It
   presents as a hung GPU. Here the original blocker was the Samsung
   umts_boot0 modem-boot device, opened by the vendor cass daemon before
   the CP is booted. The lookup stays under the mutex; the driver open
   runs without it.

2. MISCDBG tracing. printks around the lock, the drop, the driver-open
   call and its return. Without them the holder is invisible: it spins
   R-state, so it never matches a wchan or D-state sweep, its
   /proc/PID/stack is unreadable while running, and a task blocked inside
   ->open() has no fd for the device yet. Two sessions failed to find it
   by inference; these printks named it in one boot.

The 2015 LKML patch proposing the same scope change upstream was never
merged, so this is a deliberate local deviation rather than a backport.

Boot-tested: this is the kernel the device runs. Kept in
patches-experimental only because the tracing is too noisy for a release
build - split the printks out before promoting the scope fix.
---
diff --git a/drivers/char/misc.c b/drivers/char/misc.c
index ee104af50..6b14333d0 100644
--- a/drivers/char/misc.c
+++ b/drivers/char/misc.c
@@ -117,26 +117,46 @@ static int misc_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 	int err = -ENODEV;
 	const struct file_operations *new_fops = NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * a50: call the driver's open() OUTSIDE the global misc_mtx. Stock
+	 * behaviour (mainline 4.14 and later alike) holds the mutex across
+	 * f_op->open, so a driver whose open blocks forever - here: the
+	 * Samsung umts_boot0 modem-boot device, opened by the vendor cass
+	 * daemon before the CP is booted - freezes every misc open on the
+	 * system (mali0, ion, binder, ...), taking the whole display stack
+	 * with it (observed 2026-09-02/03). Lookup stays under the mutex;
+	 * the driver open runs without it.
+	 */
 	mutex_lock(&misc_mtx);
-
+	printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s GOTLOCK minor=%d\n",
+	       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 	list_for_each_entry(c, &misc_list, list) {
 		if (c->minor == minor) {
 			new_fops = fops_get(c->fops);
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+	mutex_unlock(&misc_mtx);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s DROPPED minor=%d\n",
+	       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 
 	if (!new_fops) {
-		mutex_unlock(&misc_mtx);
+		printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s REQMOD minor=%d\n",
+		       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 		request_module("char-major-%d-%d", MISC_MAJOR, minor);
-		mutex_lock(&misc_mtx);
+		printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s REQMOD-DONE minor=%d\n",
+		       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 
+		mutex_lock(&misc_mtx);
+		printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s GOTLOCK2 minor=%d\n",
+		       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 		list_for_each_entry(c, &misc_list, list) {
 			if (c->minor == minor) {
 				new_fops = fops_get(c->fops);
 				break;
 			}
 		}
+		mutex_unlock(&misc_mtx);
 		if (!new_fops)
 			goto fail;
 	}
@@ -150,10 +170,13 @@ static int misc_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 
 	err = 0;
 	replace_fops(file, new_fops);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s CALLING-DRIVER-OPEN minor=%d\n",
+	       current->pid, current->comm, minor);
 	if (file->f_op->open)
 		err = file->f_op->open(inode, file);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "MISCDBG: pid=%d comm=%s DRIVER-OPEN-RETURNED minor=%d err=%d\n",
+	       current->pid, current->comm, minor, err);
 fail:
-	mutex_unlock(&misc_mtx);
 	return err;
 }
 
--
2.43.0

